\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Geometry of the critical-pressure region $\Omega _{\rm  crit}$ in the early remnant. The cage of rings is the $P=p_{\rm  crit}$ surface of the oblate remnant core. The equatorial cut shows the two congruent lobes of the rotating $m=2$ double-core pattern (taiji shape); the two tones only distinguish the lobes, which hold the same metastable nuclear matter. Each lobe carries one of the pre-merger quark cores (shaded spheres, drawn to scale for $R_0=1\,\text  {km}$ and $R_{\rm  lobe}=3\,\text  {km}$). Over the emission window the conversion front advances each core boundary by only $u(0^-)\,\Delta t_{\rm  pm}\approx 10\,\text  {m}$.}}{2}{}}
\newlabel{fig:omega_crit_geom}{{1}{2}{}{}{}}
